vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38530/selection/ma-v1/399476c63490a1635317a2edec2f4249e39877e6f2373240baf341fcd4d26fe5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441/selection/8365d4f0589b34019196521a7fdf97bd92dd8232cf8ca267fe58abdfd86d53b2" :answer/id #uuid "c4d44ae6-e9d7-547a-b062-87f77aef76da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441/selection/4f25deac0ad0a23df4d205e54f69658f04744e31fecd2f3205bdc41e192b13e2" :answer/id #uuid "a178be3c-a07f-529a-984a-d3103bb73369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441/selection/42f0dcb0c948293f6fcfe41dd7ba5bb6fa134c316947bbb6ef0072bd6047fcd7" :answer/id #uuid "8b779c74-6f76-5eb0-81c3-37d002687185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441/selection/ea2fe1d8758fd805b5f76588d0a89588d9ede24f1a2278f09a3dadf648189d50" :answer/id #uuid "7c84edd3-624a-5ccf-a2e7-129048e9bde7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441/selection/93bba76f2a0c81e5d5d33fcf5f748ba4cb630121abfc39b5f29bf79f23fc037f" :answer/id #uuid "31377a3b-29e5-59ac-b6c3-61e4d6a980ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77f5f3d0-7076-51ad-bb82-2b05b0ae1d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140441/selection/8365d4f0589b34019196521a7fdf97bd92dd8232cf8ca267fe58abdfd86d53b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-140441/selection/8365d4f0589b34019196521a7fdf97bd92dd8232cf8ca267fe58abdfd86d53b2" "q-140441/selection/4f25deac0ad0a23df4d205e54f69658f04744e31fecd2f3205bdc41e192b13e2" "q-140441/selection/42f0dcb0c948293f6fcfe41dd7ba5bb6fa134c316947bbb6ef0072bd6047fcd7" "q-140441/selection/ea2fe1d8758fd805b5f76588d0a89588d9ede24f1a2278f09a3dadf648189d50" "q-140441/selection/93bba76f2a0c81e5d5d33fcf5f748ba4cb630121abfc39b5f29bf79f23fc037f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140441" :question/id #uuid "3c5b8550-93bd-5bca-bdbb-d5d6c011cb4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140441" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140441/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140441"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572/selection/73cb631369bfe2b6cd39997615e507b7b909650089f19caf0fb0285ffe8757cb" :answer/id #uuid "817b0335-0543-50d5-8c8f-d2cefdb8c105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -11 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572/selection/162425cc6d17a2867af745a3366e6d8604df797d99ccdb45b8c6303484fa4d08" :answer/id #uuid "87fce1ef-36cd-5441-954f-790e0ffbecfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -3 \\\\ 12 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572/selection/0f6844a7639b1527d3a09ef53c0d62830cccce455d4a7633f30c7b1bea9fbd43" :answer/id #uuid "f3ce5ea6-7f4f-532e-92b4-83e9e6116364" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572/selection/ce37252b874d2f0bc156ed264540b189063ae29fd909e3b44f4f0cd3189cfd62" :answer/id #uuid "72f76471-7cc5-5d07-b8ff-5af3ed320d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572/selection/4cdc41e7ee3fc74a036e571069f24f26c2ce32d4a3a9de8f79be967c8a462a31" :answer/id #uuid "f9c7df68-ab29-50ec-921a-5951dabc6702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2086c6ff-be93-540d-88e0-3990791946e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97572/selection/ce37252b874d2f0bc156ed264540b189063ae29fd909e3b44f4f0cd3189cfd62" :answer-field/choices ["q-97572/selection/73cb631369bfe2b6cd39997615e507b7b909650089f19caf0fb0285ffe8757cb" "q-97572/selection/162425cc6d17a2867af745a3366e6d8604df797d99ccdb45b8c6303484fa4d08" "q-97572/selection/0f6844a7639b1527d3a09ef53c0d62830cccce455d4a7633f30c7b1bea9fbd43" "q-97572/selection/ce37252b874d2f0bc156ed264540b189063ae29fd909e3b44f4f0cd3189cfd62" "q-97572/selection/4cdc41e7ee3fc74a036e571069f24f26c2ce32d4a3a9de8f79be967c8a462a31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97572" :question/id #uuid "ee3204a4-be4d-5c58-b438-f3f6116c56d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97572" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97572/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97572"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97549/selection/cfc9fe602bd8c01919236e26f04ddb1c6480c191cde9662160094759f5f69364" :answer/id #uuid "f54f733a-06f1-57d3-9abe-024a54762a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97549/selection/bbecaf1ca4467bfc8ebca9a643c8d408c32ed1edcbed866da928b6e4cfb9b627" :answer/id #uuid "f5c68aa0-d239-5bd1-bea9-59ba078bf6e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97549/selection/1113eb269142eada6554e27bfe7d09afe92e8652bcc1e6a0a06442cbe4b64c5e" :answer/id #uuid "80d8a130-e4bf-5365-a759-4ca40e313501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/val