ed}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97549/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97549"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97546/selection/c8b8280cb84f9bbe1360e48ffe9bf8d3f7144f6d336be790ca0aefc25a86d546" :answer/id #uuid "01f2d3bf-6dfc-543a-9f3a-13351e096fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 7 & 27 \\\\ -10 & -20 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97546/selection/c42f6803a00d3a119e563d8ea6967af5b2c8a30207b42c9fbcaacb48d633d1fb" :answer/id #uuid "5e800eba-550a-59ca-af39-1c68062c95ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :