9ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97547" :question/id #uuid "9ad57989-7a79-5aa3-aa45-200ce4a5483e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97547" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{3})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97547/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97579/selection/1e4b7e8ea2a18a9ebf9651a9530f62a82b9c6b91284e4d886bf97f23c94fc0ea" :answer/id #uuid "f41024b9-c000-53b9-9215-4f20b41b2777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97579/selection/09813ccd368e6d54befef11731c3c2f29db98427ee50743618a4aa28cba54044" :answer/id #uuid "081064af-3e0a-578c-93af-2079c3298952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97579/selection/1798577a5fd9e7d5e87ac0b4a0c282029c832cc07998196cf6713927ba4a88f3" :answer/id #uuid "3a15d17b-f6d1-53a4-87fe-cdac33f555d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97579/selection/697be4c47645dae652e5713ca44d06ce137d85324fb876480341fdef0fcab139" :answer/id #uuid "8c8333d3-2ec5-5285-826c-9a6a363e0753" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97579/selection/eead5618cc48364ad8f18c35fbdc62fc7dfc1e5ee6a234b47963f34143751b66" :answer/id #uuid "19c81ff5-4b1b-54da-baad-30c28b96bab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97579/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee44b5f-37e6-5398-867c-dcd4a69352b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97579/selection/1e4b7e8ea2a18a9ebf9651a9530f62a82b9c6b91284e4d886bf97f23c94fc0ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-97579/selection/1e4b7e8ea2a18a9ebf965