ively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38865/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38865"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584/selection/8038d6f923a3bb35c4444e90ef02846047ab2f3fbebd366a16a3e0ac17ed6e48" :answer/id #uuid "bc1a42d2-a220-5297-8af8-339f02507cec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584/selection/7b381bc88f0440f56acc91942637426c2e7b6d4a110d16a6856387c7deb8ae51" :answer/id #uuid "0810e492-7ef0-599b-93d0-7c0f55f92d34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584/selection/d0ed1e643738d34ce6194ef8c02c842d266197eb600b5e66cbc9af2aa1107680" :answer/id #uuid "7e7259de-fc46-5989-9bf7-caee5ccaee30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584/selection/49d547fb441fbfa4bcfa10c4d502e51468551627dd95ebb17f55ee957a0025ed" :answer/id #uuid "3f651f01-d31f-5739-b15b-825dfa9c2704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584/selection/0a7b5b283e6f81ec5072ba723e5baf88630db04f14141148b9124b712ec976db" :answer/id #uuid "58f62d00-5c59-59e6-9f02-b0290bb8035a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6dac780-a859-5182-8a5a-47370bba729a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97584/selection/49d547fb441fbfa4bcfa10c4d502e51468551627dd95ebb17f55ee957a0025ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-97584/selection/8038d6f923a3bb35c4444e90ef02846047ab2f3fbebd366a16a3e0ac17ed6e48" "q-97584/selection/7b381bc88f0440f56acc91942637426c2e7b6d4a110d16a6856387c7deb8ae51" "q-97584/selection/d0ed1e643738d34ce6194ef8c02c842d266197eb600b5e66cbc9af2aa1107680" "q-97584/selection/49d547fb441fbfa4bcfa10c4d502e51468551627dd95ebb17f55ee957a0025ed" "q-97584/selection/0a7b5b283e6f81ec5072ba723e5baf88630db04f14141148b9124b712ec976db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97584" :question/id #uuid "640c6e88-9d5b-5059-b700-19a8b1d26da1" :question/math-academy-id "q-97584" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97584/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588/selection/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" :answer/id #uuid "066d82f9-8b3e-5206-92c1-af8a908d4082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588/selection/6aff2f1b920a43b6cab44edff5ca17f4d645ac1d728b18701bda7cdc8f30d866" :answer/id #uuid "9f2be7d8-1087-51de-ba3d-497da290d3aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588/selection/db1cdefaf88b6b20702b9b0b69c8e4d9215dd4ac80e8142de629a64a968ebb0c" :answer/id #uuid "9237ea21-9bfb-5bea-bd6d-73c169ab5d68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588/selection/ea64812ce7141a7a7d2f8af22dc687cce874349f3f0802fffb9a23879896c638" :answer/id #uuid "0725d705-073d-52f5-bd6c-76a9db041d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588/selection/8dceadc03067f1b2ad28b56352d2984806f1344bb996c8de07ef85ad1b17abf2" :answer/id #uuid "e062d0a7-6e98-52c9-82a2-53a3795d7edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c952e52-2cfd-5861-b960-a4a64f66b375" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97588/selection/ea64812ce7141a7a7d2f8af22dc687cce874349f3f0802fffb9a23879896c638" :answer-field/choices ["q-97588/selection/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" "q-97588/selection/6aff2f1b920a43b6cab44edff5ca17f4d645ac1d728b18701bda7cdc8f30d866" "q-97588/selection/db1cdefaf88b6b20702b9b0b69c8e4d9215dd4ac80e8142de629a64a968ebb0c" "q-97588/selection/ea64812ce7141a7a7d2f8af22dc687cce874349f3f0802fffb9a23879896c638" "q-97588/selection/8dceadc03067f1b2ad28b56352d2984806f1344bb996c8de07ef85ad1b17abf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97588" :question/id #uuid "5a1af09a-7369-5e69-a1b2-09373ab32df5" :question/math-academy-id "q-97588" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97588/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446/selection/a47b11bfac40f0186de40efa841e96bd61f01cc7289567726de7ad745dc041ac" :answer/id #uuid "dfe8b6e5-bcea-5457-9d87-891bb6cf5360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446/selection/5e41d86ebe485194900ca1001568aae2f309ed4619096f2bebdc22835331cd9e" :answer/id #uuid "481fdeb6-5f97-5658-8f34-864e77552c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446/selection/5c76cde10c7797b452d562127cce56fdccb7d678aa421e3cd3fff5ba463ae045" :answer/id #uuid "154bf734-4b6e-53dc-b46e-1652fe7adfd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446/selection/455d54b193ea82449604662e36a1b7429ffe85880718d2cd963caf897f7acf23" :answer/id #uuid "83a05bf5-09e3-5cf6-9a96-e23b3e2e6af1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446/selection/2a744a76e8c8f4fb67a36fb24d7fa3207f77c084b739ba903354af9f8231edec" :answer/id #uuid "9ca59c40-b575-5fb8-859b-a5d4adc494bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 76 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ec63fa-aed8-5cd9-acf8-5502688e3186" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140446/selection/5c76cde10c7797b452d562127cce56fdccb7d678aa421e3cd3fff5ba463ae045" :answer-field/choices ["q-140446/selection/a47b11bfac40f0186de40efa841e96bd61f01cc7289567726de7ad745dc041ac" "q-140446/selection/5e41d86ebe485194900ca1001568aae2f309ed4619096f2bebdc22835331cd9e" "q-140446/selection/5c76cde10c7797b452d562127cce56fdccb7d678aa421e3cd3fff5ba463ae045" "q-140446/selection/455d54b193ea82449604662e36a1b7429ffe85880718d2cd963caf897f7acf23" "q-140446/selection/2a744a76e8c8f4fb67a36fb24d7fa3207f77c084b739ba903354af9f8231edec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140446" :question/id #uuid "1b32c830-750d-503e-9a1d-be23af443696" :question/math-academy-id "q-140446" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-15 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -15 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 15\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 80 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140446/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140446"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583/selection/ad7f241f53510a9ca0600dbdca258328e851b2e62dec9574f1c76c7377a985f4" :answer/id #uuid "05d4cb5d-df13-53c1-92fa-e9a162c673ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583/selection/292e5c78467babaedb9dd895dc3050f7f138155e3a8ee493d80d12c9a172aaf2" :answer/id #uuid "e127cb80-0d0c-5c09-bd43-3823e3e330f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583/selection/fe496bd08a5896360631a23c8681f6def71c47cb9a9e8848a87e110d3dbd582d" :answer/id #uuid "8570f05d-0e31-5c77-bc90-c91c0bd043f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583/selection/950be6f481e1f969a05e7582d6739653d4fcebf1de430c71a9ce10af90c9e373" :answer/id #uuid "c08e2385-b8f9-54e6-b415-a2d014aa819a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583/selection/b67e636ea15629ca59241b34ee7da38029123c7a89b7fe01ddab1b311af65fd5" :answer/id #uuid "5f3b1c53-7659-5b55-a2d1-22f6bf38ffcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe057ce2-70b5-5f38-8543-580eca972165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97583/selection/b67e636ea15629ca59241b34ee7da38029123c7a89b7fe01ddab1b311af65fd5" :answer-field/choices ["q-97583/selection/ad7f241f53510a9ca0600dbdca258328e851b2e62dec9574f1c76c7377a985f4" "q-97583/selection/292e5c78467babaedb9dd895dc3050f7f138155e3a8ee493d80d12c9a172aaf2" "q-97583/selection/fe496bd08a5896360631a23c8681f6def71c47cb9a9e8848a87e110d3dbd582d" "q-97583/selection/950be6f481e1f969a05e7582d6739653d4fcebf1de430c71a9ce10af90c9e373" "q-97583/selection/b67e636ea15629ca59241b34ee7da38029123c7a89b7fe01ddab1b311af65fd5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97583" :question/id #uuid "473ad29f-d952-5261-9293-cd15e4622b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-97583" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97583/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-97587"] :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8604"] :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf{T} : V \\rightarrow W$ is a linear map and $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\}$ and $\\mathcal{C} = \\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. Find the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1)=-3\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2,\\quad$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)=\\mathbf{c}_2-2\\mathbf{c}_1\\quad$ and $\\quad\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)=\\mathbf{c}_1+5\\mathbf{c}_2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{2}-2{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})={c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2)$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/215cd69925ccfeab3ccb20874b7cdc2d837b99f33d8112f95fa5d2b646a27d40.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8605"] :question/problem "Consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{\\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/7c123e6f7d842a8e86e4c99826d25df070982514960752a25481a9f3f046cc1b.png)\n\nFind the matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ relative to these bases if \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/9a469219c661453d7891935b2ef0a32bff972bcf903d641ca7e31b7bec26369a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_1),$ $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_2),$ and $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_3)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{b}_i)$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ for each $i=1,2,3.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/9d774b5bd79f14bc31e88a649fcb2a682d94ae3dd8acde5e25f52369c136e11e.png)\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 & 3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -29 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C} \\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/778f179c4681bcdcc5a64bcd128d946a272fa869289d2c2e542df75ad05850b6.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5521"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/7d82125089d15dada1be4f8d6669b5e125da921019b3a9d27376353dcf59a090.png)\n\nSuppose $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:V \\rightarrow W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in V$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are shown above. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5522"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/8caf13cdbf21ddfb1a121ede6ec0c21da155065905547bbd86b0e52cd57141da.png)\n\nConsider the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ (shown above) and a basis $\\mathcal{C}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\nThe matrix $[\\mathbf{T}]_{\\mathcal{B}|\\mathcal{C}}$ of the linear map $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^3$ relative to these bases, and the vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2,$ are also given. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{C}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under $\\mathbf{T}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}},$ the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}.$ So, let\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/a5b6f5f41dffd99a885bb872eac6f1e6a24bd604b360256194a0bf16b32ef381.png)\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -18\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067114/assets/862742d57ad0ae4b56d6f345d825313bebf0d712f9c59ea1ed8b55d0a2eea22e.png)\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
